# Normalise every text file to LF in the repository, whatever a contributor's editor or
# git config does locally. Everything here ends up inside a Linux container, and it keeps
# diffs against the OpenMasjidDisplay / OpenMasjidDonations templates line-ending-clean.
#
# `text=auto` DETECTS text vs binary, so the PNGs under assets/ and web/public/ are left
# untouched. Without this line the attributes below cover only shell/YAML/Dockerfile, and
# a contributor on Windows with the default `core.autocrlf=true` commits CRLF blobs for
# everything else — which is exactly how the two files fixed in this commit got that way.
* text=auto eol=lf
# Be explicit for the files that must run inside the container.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
